1
00:00:03,109 --> 00:00:06,279
Noah cuts a hard-boiled egg: shell, white, yolk.

2
00:00:06,329 --> 00:00:09,165
And under our feet, what is the Earth like?

3
00:00:09,215 --> 00:00:09,634
Hollow?

4
00:00:09,684 --> 00:00:10,557
Full of lava?

5
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:12,549
Mila digs and digs…

6
00:00:12,599 --> 00:00:13,217
one meter!

7
00:00:13,267 --> 00:00:17,224
But the center of the Earth is six thousand kilometers down,

8
00:00:17,274 --> 00:00:18,677
too far for a shovel!

9
00:00:19,472 --> 00:00:20,986
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:23,502 --> 00:00:24,087
Mini mode!

11
00:00:24,137 --> 00:00:26,311
First the crust, thin like a shell.

12
00:00:26,361 --> 00:00:30,315
Then the mantle: three thousand kilometers of burning-hot rock,

13
00:00:30,365 --> 00:00:32,080
so hot it is almost melted.

14
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:36,085
At the center, the core of iron and nickel is liquid outside,

15
00:00:36,135 --> 00:00:38,347
and that is what makes the magnetic field…

16
00:00:38,397 --> 00:00:39,635
but solid at the heart.

17
00:00:40,852 --> 00:00:41,685
How do we know?

18
00:00:41,735 --> 00:00:45,277
Thanks to earthquakes, whose waves travel through the planet,

19
00:00:45,327 --> 00:00:47,573
and the liquid core stops some of them.

20
00:00:47,623 --> 00:00:49,212
It's an X-ray of the Earth!

21
00:00:50,022 --> 00:00:53,707
Curio, in mini mode, floats at the edge of the core,

22
00:00:53,757 --> 00:00:56,005
where molten metal turns slowly…

23
00:00:56,055 --> 00:00:57,133
Quick, back up!

24
00:00:57,910 --> 00:01:00,415
And that's what is hidden inside the Earth.

25
00:01:01,411 --> 00:01:04,356
Under the crust, a mantle of burning-hot rock,

26
00:01:04,406 --> 00:01:07,531
then an iron core: liquid outside, solid inside.

27
00:01:08,321 --> 00:01:10,831
With an adult: cut a hard-boiled egg.

28
00:01:10,881 --> 00:01:13,184
Its shell is the crust, the white,

29
00:01:13,234 --> 00:01:15,606
the mantle, and the yolk, the core…

30
00:01:15,656 --> 00:01:17,524
which really has two parts!

31
00:01:18,302 --> 00:01:20,463
And why do volcanoes erupt?

32
00:01:20,513 --> 00:01:22,151
The answer tomorrow.
